on"},{"sourceUnit":{"$ref":"2383"},"sourceKey":"equal","destinationUnit":{"$ref":"2373"},"destinationKey":"a","guid":"c093028b-bf87-4adf-9e1b-1fe02f11941b","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.ValueConnection"},{"sourceUnit":{"$ref":"2391"},"sourceKey":"value","destinationUnit":{"$ref":"2383"},"destinationKey":"b","guid":"28688389-95e8-4a91-92be-d662fa3b6954","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.ValueConnection"},{"sourceUnit":{"$ref":"2370"},"sourceKey":"value","destinationUnit":{"$ref":"2368"},"destinationKey":"b","guid":"109814d6-1fab-4e74-9a5f-9dff1539d262","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.ValueConnection"},{"sourceUnit":{"$ref":"2365"},"sourceKey":"value","destinationUnit":{"$ref":"2396"},"destinationKey":"b","guid":"9c697ed4-0d62-476a-8058-1c237c02a164","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.ValueConnection"},{"position":{"xMin":-1814.0,"yMin":394.0,"xMax":-1100.0,"yMax":700.0},"title":"Correct
      way to check if my AI has card in hand AND add them to possibleCards list","body":"\n1)
      Go trough my Cards In Hand (Game Objects) with For Each loop\n\n2) Get the
      Card Display component (from my Game Objects, I make a reference to the Card
      Display component which contains my Scriptable Objects)\n\n3) Get the Card
      Data component (the Card Data component is what it makes me possible to make
      a reference to my Scripting Objects from my GameObjects)\n\n4) Get Card Name
      (refers to my Scriptable Objects)\n-> This one is tricky : My Card Data component
      contains which specific Card is attached to it\nSo I can get my cards data
      (value, name, color, ...) from my Card Display component \n\n5) Connect my
